                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Rule in all three: a sheet never keeps spare room as blank space. Homework: the writing paper takes it. Question: the answer tiles take it and their numbers grow with them. Wide window: the math, the reading text and the teacher's picture are set larger.\n\nHere: your numbered lines fill the sheet as you work, so the paper shrinks to a few lines. In a wide window the teacher's answers move beside your lines and the teacher's picture sits beside the paper.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 24,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
